# Keep `COPY . .` (Dockerfile.build-context) down to the tracked tree: local
# build outputs, caches, untracked docs and the heavyweight vendored copies
# stay out of the image. The build-base image carries its own third-party
# set under /opt/simplex-thirdparty; third_party/versions and third_party/
# license are small and informative, so they stay in the context.
.git
.claude
.agents
.codex
.vscode
build*
# The release install tree (`cmake --install` with SIMPLEX_BUNDLE_RUNTIME set)
# holds a copy of every built library AND of the bundled runtime — the image
# would rebuild all of it from source, so shipping it in the context is dead
# weight measured in hundreds of megabytes.
stage
docs
third_party/include
third_party/libs
CMakeFiles
